Attempt-2 QML metadata remediation
----------------------------------

Revision 6.30.0-0supralinux2 consumed the retained Kirigami 6.30.0-0supralinux2 PASS artifact, passed 8/8 upstream tests, and passed the reviewed symbols transformation far enough for dh_makeshlibs to complete. Packaging then failed in dh_qmldeps because org.kde.kirigami was available to sbuild as a local extra package but was not installed in the build chroot: KQuickCharts did not declare the QML module as a package-build dependency.

Revision 6.30.0-0supralinux3 therefore adds qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami (>= 6.30.0~) to Build-Depends. This is a Debian/QML metadata-generation dependency required while dh_qmldeps resolves packaged imports. It does not add libkirigami-dev, does not change upstream CMake requirements, and does not create a KDE Framework build-DAG edge.

The Batch 10 runner continues to supply Kirigami only from a retained/current SupraLINUX PASS artifact and later verifies qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami at the exact campaign version. Ubuntu's older KDE package cannot satisfy the >= 6.30.0~ build floor.

Attempt-3 development-consumer remediation
------------------------------------------

Revision 6.30.0-0supralinux3 passed build, 8/8 upstream tests, Lintian, dh_qmldeps, ABI validation with the reviewed effective floor, QML import validation and exact local-package APT closure. The final consumer CMake configure then failed because the installed KF6QuickChartsConfig.cmake explicitly executes find_dependency(ECM 6.30.0), while libquickcharts-dev did not declare extra-cmake-modules as a binary development dependency.

This is an exported development-package contract from the KDE 6.30 CMake config, not a new KQuickCharts Framework build dependency. Revision 6.30.0-0supralinux4 adds extra-cmake-modules (>= 6.30.0~) to libquickcharts-dev Depends. The Batch 10 consumer gate supplies and verifies the retained SupraLINUX extra-cmake-modules 6.30.0-0supralinux3 PASS artifact, so Ubuntu's older ECM cannot silently satisfy the exported config.

The KDE Framework build dependency metadata remains unchanged: kde_framework_build_dependencies=[].
